request: Make the output easier to read. --behaviour

governor turn 1: ask  ("Easier to read" is subjective, and it could be met in several different ways. Each one changes the list output in a different way that tests would have to check. Right now `todo list` prints lines like "[ ] buy milk" with no ids or due dates. I need to know which changes the user wants before I can write a contract.)
governor asks: What would make the output easier to read? Right now `todo list` prints lines like "[ ] buy milk". It doesn't show the todo's id, which you need for `todo complete`, or its due date. Which of these do you want? (Pick any.)
(a) Show the id on each line, e.g. "#1 [ ] buy milk".
(b) Show the due date when there is one, e.g. "#1 [ ] buy milk (due 2026-11-01)".
(c) Line up the columns so titles and due dates start at the same position on every line.
(d) Show open todos first and completed ones after, or sort by due date.
(e) Add a summary line, e.g. "2 open, 1 done".
(f) Something else. Please describe it, ideally with an example of the output you'd like.
Should the "Added #N" / "Completed #N" messages also show the todo's title, e.g. "Added #1: buy milk"?

